 are ALWAYS making progress toward the next gym. Grinding/catching/detours are fine — but ONLY with a clear purpose, and then you GET BACK ON THE ROAD to Cerulean City. Never just circle the same grass. ⚠️ ORDER OF OPERATIONS: before Misty, HM Surf — the prize of the Safari Zone\'s Secret House, deep in the back area. Surf opens the sea: Cinnabar, the Seafoam route, and Victory Road\'s water — that errand comes FIRST (it unblocks the road and the trainers along it are exactly the training you need). Misty is step two, not a competing choice. Word on the road about Misty: she runs WATER-types — a whole gym over a pool; grass and electric do the work YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): You started in Pallet Town, crossed Route 1-2 and Viridian Forest, and beat Brock in Pewter City for the Boulder Badge. Now you\'re pushing on toward the next gym.. Next on my list: catch an pikachu around Viridian Forest (rare) / Power Plant later. It grows into my raichu — that\'s my answer for Misty AND Lorelei down the line. Grabbing it now, before I need it.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "Yo! Champ in the making! Let me give you some advice! The LEADER, MISTY, is a pro who uses WATER-type POK.MON. You can drain all their water with GRASS-type POK"; "Why don\'t you go upstairs and try trading POK.MON with your friends? You could get a lot more variety by trading. The POK.MON you get in trades grow quickly, to"; "Why don\'t you go upstairs and try trading POK.MON with your friends? You could get a lot more variety by trading. The POK.MON you get in trades grow quickly, to"; "That cruise ship S.S. ANNE is in VERMILION CITY. I hear there are lots of TRAINERS on board, too. They invited me to their party, but I can\'t stand fancy do\'s. ". YOUR PLAN — right now: You\'re ready — stop grinding and head to Cerulean City for the Cascade Badge. Next: You\'re ready — travel t